# Forgot Password Implementation Plan

Implement a secure and visually consistent "Forgot Password" flow using Firebase Authentication.

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> The password reset link will be sent to the user's registered email address. Ensure that the Firebase project is configured with a valid sender email in the Firebase Console (Authentication > Templates).

## Proposed Changes

### Authentication Logic

#### [NEW] [forgot_password.dart](file:///d:/FYP/vision_app/lib/pages/forgot_password.dart)
- Create a new stateful widget `ForgotPasswordPage`.
- Use the existing design system (`AppColors`, `AppTextStyles`, `GlassCard`) for a premium look.
- Implement a single email input field.
- Add a "Reset Password" button that triggers `_auth.sendPasswordResetEmail`.
- Include a "Back to Login" navigation.

### Routing

#### [MODIFY] [main.dart](file:///d:/FYP/vision_app/lib/main.dart)
- Import `ForgotPasswordPage`.
- Add the route `'/forgot-password'` to the `MaterialApp` routes map.

### UI Integration

#### [MODIFY] [login.dart](file:///d:/FYP/vision_app/lib/pages/login.dart)
- Update the "Forgot password?" `TextButton` to navigate to the new route using `Navigator.pushNamed(context, '/forgot-password')`.

## Verification Plan

### Manual Verification
- **Happy Path**: Enter a valid registered email, click "Reset Password", verify SnackBar success message, check email for the reset link.
- **Error Handling**: Enter an invalid email format and verify the error SnackBar.
- **Navigation**: Verify "Back to Login" works correctly.
- **UI Consistency**: Ensure the new page matches the glassmorphism aesthetic of the login page.
